The average passes 10% at $30,000, 20% at $45,000, 30% at $110,000 and 40% at $290,000.
It climbs more slowly than the marginal rate, because each higher rate applies only to the dollars above its bracket. At $500,000 the average is 45.88%, while the top marginal rate is 53.8%. It reaches half of its $500,000 value at $57,000.

