The reduction fades out above about $25,000, and the Canada workers benefit shrinks by 15 cents for every dollar above $27,700. The rate is 44.39% from $25,100, and 59.24% from $27,700 to $30,700, higher than the top rate of 53.8%. It eases to 43.41% from $30,800, and falls to 28.55% at $38,900 once both are gone.
It steps up to 34.3% from $45,100 (the second bracket) and 40.74% from $59,100 (the federal 20.5% bracket), then down as pension and insurance stop. The top rate in this chart is 53.8%, from $290,000, where the line goes straight. The form adds higher rates above about $564,000.

